As with any lujvo, the meaning would have to be looked up in the
dictionary. The form is available, but that doesn't mean it will be used.


My understanding of the cumulative effect of dotside is that every *name*
> must be surrounded by glottal stops
>

A common misunderstanding, but still a misunderstanding.


> (which otherwise do not except between final and initial vowels, i.e.,
> phonemically conditioned).  Thus, {.paris.rom.} is distinct from {. paris
> rom.}
>
> No, If there is no pause between "paris" and "rom" it must be written
"parisrom". If it is written "paris rom" then the pause between them is
obligatory, whether or not a dot is written.

mu'o mi'e xorxes

